.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH attachment 1  "attachment " 
.SH NAME
attachment \- Manage attachments using the shared API
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBattachment\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage attachments using the shared API.
.PP
An attachment is a binary part of a message.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
attachment\-list(1)
List the attachments carried by a single message in the active account
.TP
attachment\-download(1)
Download specific attachments of a single message to disk
.TP
attachment\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
